[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="ManualPage" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/components/manual_page.gd" id="1_page"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_page")
title = "DIAGNOSTICS"
body = "TEST POINTS. Carry a tool and press {interact} at a probe. POWER is in storage near the tools; ATMOSPHERE in the life-support side bay; WATER in the water closet; THERMAL and HULL in the engine bay.

SCANNER. Logs system wear and condition percentages. A scan is inspection, not fault diagnosis. MULTIMETER. Identifies one undiagnosed failure per interaction; repeat until clear, then read STATUS or WATCH REPORT for the component and failure mode.

EXTERNAL HARDWARE REFIT
  1  Diagnose a fault with the multimeter (or scan routine wear).
  2  Open SHIP CONTROL / POWER at the cupola wall terminal: go through the cockpit hatch, press {interact} at the pilot seat to sit, aim at the wall terminal and press {interact}. Switch OFF the service breaker named below or by the probe; SHED is not isolation. Press {leave_seat} to leave the seat. (LIGHTING alone can also be switched at the storage breaker panel.)
  3  Carry the wrench to that system's probe and press {interact}.
  4  Select OPEN [component] COVER.
  5  Select REFIT [component]. One gasket is drawn from stores; the listed service time passes while all systems keep running.
  6  Select CLOSE [component] COVER. Dismiss with {close}.
  7  Return to the same terminal and restore the breaker. Check STATUS: failure cleared, service restored, readings recovering. A refit improves condition; it does not make old hardware new.

SERVICE BREAKERS. LIGHTING BALLAST: LIGHTING. WATER PUMP MAIN and HEATER MAIN: LIFE SUPPORT (the heater loses power while it is off: fetch the wrench BEFORE switching it off, then go straight to the probe and restore it promptly. The ship cools quickly but recovers within hours). SCRUBBER BLOWER: SCRUBBER. RTG and BATTERY: ALL bus breakers OFF, not just lighting. HULL seam fittings: no service breaker.

STOCK. Check STORES before opening equipment. Refits use one gasket each, automatically from inventory, not a carried loose part. Missing gasket: use the engine-bay fabricator's gasket recipe if materials remain.

FILTERS / PUNCTURES. A blower refit is not a filter swap; see LIFE SUPPORT. A hull seam refit does not patch a puncture; use the leaking room's patch point, DAMAGE CONTROL.

PROPULSION. Separate stern EVA panels have their own isolation, tool changes and restore steps; see PROPULSION. Never open the sealed drive core."
